.TH CWHIP 1 "2026" "cwhip 0.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cwhip \- compiler for the Cwhip programming language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cwhip
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIinput\fR...
.br
.B cwhip
\-\-print\-paths [\fB\-M\fR \fIdir\fR] [\fIinput\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cwhip
compiles Cwhip source files ending in
.IR .cw .
to LLVM IR and invokes
.BR clang (1)
to produce an executable, or a relocatable object with
.BR \-c .
Object inputs
.RI ( .o ,
.IR .obj )
are linked with the generated code. Exactly one source input must contain the
top\-level
.B start
block when an executable is produced.
.PP
The compiler is relocatable: it locates its runtime library, runtime headers,
String builtin, and standard modules relative to its own executable, so an
installed tree may be moved as a unit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print option help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the compiler version and exit.
.TP
.B \-v
Increase verbosity; may be repeated or grouped
.RB ( \-vv ,
.BR \-vvv ).
Level 1 reports compiler phases, level 2 also prints every resolved path and
the exact
.B clang
commands, and level 3 adds per\-phase timings. All verbose output goes to
standard error.
.TP
.BI \-\-verbosity= N
Set the verbosity level directly (0 to 3). It cannot be combined with
.BR \-v .
Levels above 3 are rejected.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-trace =\fItarget\fR[,\fItarget\fR...]
Trace compiler internals. Targets are
.BR scanner ,
.BR parser ,
.BR ast ,
and
.BR symbols ;
they are case\-insensitive and may be given as a comma\-separated list or by
repeating the option. Scanner and parser traces go to standard error; the AST
and symbol table are printed to standard output.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-paths
Print the resolved executable, prefix, runtime directory and library, include
directory, builtin, discovered project root and lock, every package root with
its origin and precedence, and the
.B clang
executable, then exit successfully. No input is required.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-only
Parse and check the source inputs without generating code.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-compile\-only
Compile the source inputs to one relocatable object without linking.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-debug
Emit DWARF debug information.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIfile\fR"
Write the executable or object to
.IR file .
.TP
.BI \-\-emit\-llvm " file"
Also save the generated LLVM IR to
.IR file .
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-path " \fIdir\fR[:\fIdir\fR...]"
Add directories to the textual include search path.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-include\-depth " n"
Limit nested textual includes (default 16).
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-module\-dir " \fIdir\fR"
Add
.I dir
as the highest-priority package storage root. The directory must exist; it does
not relocate the discovered project's manifest or lock.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-library\-path " \fIdir\fR"
Add a linker search directory.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-library " \fIname\fR"
Link with library
.IR name .
.SH MODULES
An
.B import
resolves a package from
.IR root / name / version /cwhip\-package.toml .
Package roots are searched in this order:
.IP 1. 4
The CLI root given by
.BR \-M .
.IP 2. 4
The discovered project's
.IR project\-root /modules
directory. Project discovery starts at the first source parent (or current
directory without source input) and selects the nearest ancestor containing
.I cwhip-pkg.toml
or a
.I modules
directory. Without a marker, the source parent is used.
.IP 3. 4
The environment root
.BR CWHIP_MODULE_DIR .
.IP 4. 4
The user root
.IR <config\-home>/cwhip/modules ,
normally
.IR ~/.config/cwhip/modules .
When
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is set, it is used as the config home and must be absolute.
.IP 5. 4
The standard module directory shipped with the compiler, normally
.IR <prefix>/share/cwhip/modules .
.PP
The first module root containing a package shadows lower\-priority roots. Without
a project lock, the highest stable version is selected only from the versions
in that root. The CLI and environment roots must exist; absent project and user
roots are optional.
.PP
New projects use cwhip-pkg.toml for direct dependencies and cwhip-pkg.lock for the
complete exact graph. The manifest and lock are always discovered from the
source project and cannot be relocated by \-M or CWHIP_MODULE_DIR.
The compiler checks the lock schema, manifest freshness, selected package
contents, and graph edges without network access. Missing or invalid locks
are errors. Imports absent from the lock are rejected. A package found in an
override root must match the locked version, edges, and content hash; an invalid
higher\-priority candidate is not silently bypassed.
Use cwhip-pkg init, cwhip-pkg add OWNER/REPO \-\-yes, and cwhip-pkg install \-\-yes;
ordinary compilation does not require evaluating cwhip-pkg env.
.PP
The legacy \-\-package\-path, CWHIP_PACKAGE_PATH, CWHIP_MODULE_REGISTRY,
./cwhip-modules.tsv, and modules/modules.toml mechanisms are removed.
.PP
An unaliased import binds the manifest's declared export name; import system
exposes System.Process. An explicit import system as Sys exposes Sys.Process
instead. Colliding bindings are errors. String remains an implicit prelude.
.PP
When a module cannot be found, the diagnostic lists every module root and
its origin.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CWHIP_MODULE_DIR
Additional package storage root searched after the discovered project root and
before user and installation roots. A set but missing directory is an error.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Absolute user config directory; user packages are searched in
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cwhip/modules .
Defaults to
.IR ~/.config/cwhip/modules .
.TP
.B CWHIP_HOME
Installation prefix used instead of the executable location.
.TP
.BR CWHIP_RUNTIME_DIR ", " CWHIP_INCLUDE_DIR ", " CWHIP_BUILTIN_DIR ", " CWHIP_STDLIB_MODULE_DIR
Override individual resource directories; each takes precedence over
.BR CWHIP_HOME .
.TP
.B CC
C compiler driver used instead of the configured
.BR clang .
.SH FILES
Paths are relative to the installation prefix (the parent of the
.I bin
directory holding
.BR cwhip ).
.TP
.I bin/cwhip
The compiler.
.TP
.I lib/cwhip/libcwhip_runtime.a
The garbage\-collected runtime linked into every executable.
.TP
.I include/cwhip/
Runtime C headers used by inline C shims.
.TP
.I share/cwhip/builtin/String.cw
The String builtin.
.TP
.I share/cwhip/modules/
Standard modules.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success (including \-\-help, \-\-version, and \-\-print\-paths);
non\-zero on failure. Invalid command lines and unreadable inputs exit with 2.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cwhip hello.cw
cwhip \-vv \-M ./deps app/main.cw \-o app
cwhip \-t parser,symbols \-\-check\-only main.cw
cwhip \-\-print\-paths
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR clang (1)
